      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>Temperature control is the most checked thing in a UK kitchen. It is also the most filled in afterwards. Fridges at open and close. Cooking probes. Hot holding. Cool-down at night. Together they are the record an Environmental Health Officer reads first. So the question is whether the reading is logged when the probe comes out, or written up after close from memory.</p>"
