      "html": "<h3>What temperature should a commercial fridge be in the UK?</h3><p>The law says chilled food that needs temperature control is held at or below 8C. Many kitchens run fridges colder, often 1C to 4C, so a small drift does not break the limit. Check current FSA guidance and the HACCP plan. This is not legal advice.</p><h3>What core temperature should food be cooked to?</h3><p>Commonly 75C for 30 seconds, or an equal time and temperature, such as 70C for two minutes or 80C for six seconds. Hot food held for service stays at or above 63C. Follow current FSA guidance.</p><h3>Can I log kitchen temperatures in WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Each check arrives as a message. You reply with the reading, a voice note or a photo of the probe. The log is written for you with the time. A reading that is out of limit is flagged at once.</p><h3>Does a log app replace a probe thermometer?</h3><p>No. Quickler records the reading you take with your own calibrated probe or fridge thermometer. It adds the time and, if useful, a photo. It does not measure anything and does not keep the fridge cold.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/food-safety-audit-app-uk.html\">Food safety audit app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/haccp-checklist-app-uk.html\">HACCP checklist app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/due-diligence-food-hygiene-uk.html\">Food hygiene due diligence records</a></li></ul>"
